QUOTED NEWS EXCERPTS
data/cases/ and data/fool_deck/ contain short excerpts from published reporting
and public statements by NPR, New Jersey Monitor, the New Jersey Board of
Public Utilities, New Jersey 101.5, WHYY, Texas Public Radio and OPB (some
carrying Associated Press material). Each excerpt is attributed and linked to
its source; docs/CONTENT_SOURCES.md lists every one. These excerpts remain the
property of their publishers and are used in short form for commentary and
education.

New Jersey Monitor content is licensed CC BY-NC-ND 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/). We use short,
attributed excerpts with links and do not publish modified versions of its
articles under its name.

DOCTORED POSTS
Doctored posts in this game are deliberately altered training material for a
media-literacy game. They are posted only by made-up accounts and are stamped
as doctored when revealed. They do not represent the views or the actual
words of any outlet or person. Do not reuse them outside the game.

DATA
Electricity prices come from the U.S. Energy Information Administration
(EIA). Food prices are Bureau of Labor Statistics average prices, retrieved
through FRED (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis). U.S. government data is in
the public domain; FRED's terms of use apply to the retrieved series.
